    <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:20px">About</p>
    <h2 class="about__lede">I study computer science and public health at Stetson, with a minor in civic engagement. My work sits where they meet: <em>information that matters but is hard to use.</em></h2>
    <p class="about__body">In each role below I started by learning what the people using the data needed. Then I built the smallest thing that answered it, tested it, and wrote down where it stops being reliable.</p>
    <div class="ai-note">
      <h3>How AI fits into my workflow</h3>
      <p>AI is part of how I build. I use coding agents for implementation and code review, and I run them inside harnesses with feedback loops so they check their own work and each other’s. For a bug fix, the agent first writes a test that reproduces the bug and fails, so it can’t claim to fix something it never reproduced.</p>
      <p>Nothing is accepted on trust. I review and test every change myself, rely on end-to-end tests that show real behavior, and remove the low-value tests agents tend to pile up.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
